  "findings": [
    {
      "topic": "FoodOn formal restriction",
      "prior_judgment_qualified": "The prior receipt treated unsupported food-additive use as a prerequisite for the broader material anchor.",
      "current_judgment": "The actual member_of existential is a formal axiom, and its omission was a real review-coverage defect. FoodOn’s official guide identifies this relation as external product-category association. It is neither a has-role relation nor an assertion that the material is itself a subclass/instance of the agency category. Thus actual food use, certification, assay or regulatory approval is not established or required by that inference. MIM broadMatch is not OWL subsumption. The stronger prior food-use blocker is withdrawn; the old finding and exact evidence remain preserved.",
      "finding_id": "W05-PARENTS-NEW01"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Generic Peptone direct term",
      "prior_judgment_qualified": "The prior receipt preferred broader D011492 because assigned source observations lacked acid/enzyme and precipitation assay details.",
      "current_judgment": "D010461 has explicit Peptone entry term and the ordinary generic partial-protein-hydrolysate sense. Manufacturer wording confirms that material sense. Under current section3(4), genuinely unspecified generic Peptone should use that direct term when no independent source evidence establishes a different specified material. Requiring new lot precipitation or process tests was excessive. Manufacturer mention of base hydrolysis remains a real terminology caveat; it does not establish a base-only or contradicting actual preparation in these two observations. An exact generic mapping must not assert measured lot properties or select a branded/enzyme-specific product."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Named Polypeptone",
      "current_judgment": "The source-qualified named preparation remains distinct from the whole generic class. Local kgmicrobe.ingredient:polypeptone plus NARROW_MATCH to mesh:D010461 is supported as the closest reviewed material anchor. Preserve eight alias rejections, supplied-state/source distinctions, historical135 statistics and role/quantity holds. D011492 remains a supported broader alternative, not the closest selected anchor. No MeSH subclass edge between the sibling descriptors is asserted."
    }
  ],
